[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232838820","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122235#issuecomment-5232838820","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122235","id":5232838820,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN-bIpA","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T17:40:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T17:40:18Z","body":"Yes, I saw the code and it is a good optimization, but perhaps some of us would agree that the ability to disable warnings highlights should be independent from the script editor's theme.\r\n\r\nBut then again, that may be for the entire \"warning highlight\" feature, not just the squiggly lines...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232838820/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233157309","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122235#issuecomment-5233157309","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122235","id":5233157309,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN-ukvQ","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T18:30:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T18:30:19Z","body":"> I'm also not a _huge_ fan of introducing a feature and then implying/stating \"it's gonna slow down your computer, turn it off if you want your computer to run better\", so I could probably go about 50/50 on removing that sentence.\r\n\r\nIdk, I think it depends on the user's exposure to software like VSCode that has these squiggles. If they're a new user of Godot (therefore they don't know the comparison to previous versions or what was added) and have never used VSCode (or even a IDE lol), they might not realize that the underlines are causing it and think the entire Script Editor and Godot itself is borked. For those people, this setting would be hard to find. (Sure you can just search \"underline\" up, but they have to know that's the culprit first.)\r\n\r\nBut it's unlikely that most users are using very low-end hardware, so the sentence might not be necessary. The OP of the issue was using the web editor, so maybe there should be a setting override for the web to set the color to `0` to help mitigate this for users on startup? Same for `Android`, if there might be issues there, too. So that way, the sentence will not be needed. Instead a note can be added to the overrides explaining why this was done instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233157309/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242291197","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122235#issuecomment-5242291197","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122235","id":5242291197,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOHcD_Q","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T15:22:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T15:22:02Z","body":"Thanks for the review and suggestion! I agree it's a good idea to look into other things, and that the squiggle algorithm shouldn't be causing _this_ level of slowdown. Today I'm planning to try and get profiling for Godot set up on my computer so I can analyze the amount of time various parts of the drawing process take and determine where it spends the most time, then focus my efforts there. 😄 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242291197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]